1
00:00:00,458 --> 00:00:03,750
What is radiation therapy 
and what to expect?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:05,625
Introduction

3
00:00:05,625 --> 00:00:09,708
While you may have heard of chemotherapy
and surgery to treat cancer,

4
00:00:09,708 --> 00:00:12,500
Radiation therapy is often less well known

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,833
and talked about far
less in popular media.

6
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:20,625
This video will discuss what external beam
radiation therapy is, its role in

7
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:25,708
treating cancer, and what you can expect
in your radiation treatment journey.

8
00:00:26,125 --> 00:00:29,750
Cancer occurs when cells in your body
start to grow too fast

9
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:34,875
and in an uncontrolled way, without any
checks or balances on their growth.

10
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:38,541
The unchecked growth of these cells
lead to tumors that cause symptoms

11
00:00:38,541 --> 00:00:43,708
you may be feeling or cause your otherwise
healthy organs to malfunction.

12
00:00:44,041 --> 00:00:48,416
There are three main tools that doctors
use to combat the cancer cells

13
00:00:48,416 --> 00:00:52,166
to stop them from growing,
or to kill them all together.

14
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:56,833
These are One: Systemic Treatments,
which go throughout your body

15
00:00:56,833 --> 00:01:00,500
system, such as chemotherapy
or immunotherapy.

16
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,125
Two: Surgery and three: Radiation.

17
00:01:05,458 --> 00:01:08,291
Chemotherapy uses medications or

18
00:01:08,291 --> 00:01:11,541
 chemical compounds
to kill the unwanted cancer cells,

19
00:01:11,541 --> 00:01:13,958
and immunotherapy boosts your body's 

20
00:01:13,958 --> 00:01:16,125
own immune system to fight the cancer.

21
00:01:16,208 --> 00:01:19,083
Targeted drugs are precision treatments

22
00:01:19,208 --> 00:01:23,625
that single out specific molecular components important to cancer cell growth. 

23
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:30,000
Surgery is the physical removal
of those cells from the body.
